{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789833922,"nonce":"b2KhOcUYccqPNhDFrC6Z034kw1w=","title":"Reachability scans every function's name per call by symbol","message":"`dce::reachable_from_roots` handled a `HirCallable::Symbol` call site by\niterating the whole function table and resolving each function's name\nthrough the interner, once per such call site. A Python program's\nlibrary calls its runtime symbols from hundreds of sites, so the two\nreachability passes of a compile cost 11 ms on richards (NUC, x86_64),\n9% of start-up in a sample.\n\nFix: the module's own functions are indexed by name once per walk, at\nthe first call by symbol.","files":null}]}